Keep invalid draft distributions out of block verification and out of residual
resampling.

A NaN or +inf proposal has no usable probability ratio, and has to survive the
reductions as invalid rather than be masked away like a legitimate -inf. Block
verification looks ahead, so the whole proposal block is discarded; the bonus
row, which has no cumulative ratio, carries the request's flag. With the
proposals zeroed, the target sampler is reused directly instead of a residual
distribution that does not exist.

